The fact-check confirms that Imran Khan publicly criticized Emmanuel Macron’s comments on Islam in October 2020, but no official French government statement, press release, or diplomatic note attributes any visa cancellations or deportations of Pakistani citizens to that criticism. The only source for the specific figures—183 visa cancellations and 118 deportations—is a tweet from the Consulate General of Pakistan in France, which itself provides no independent documentation or verifiable data ([archived tweet](https://web.archive.org/web/20210629013122/https://twitter.com/PakConsulateFr/status/1322495811993903104)). No other supporting or refuting evidence was found in the record. Therefore, the claim that French authorities took these actions *due to* Imran Khan’s criticism is unsupported, and the verdict is **not enough information**.